      "side": 1,
      "message": "Okay, new problem: The code currently works as-is for the dynamic rendering path, but this is the blocker for the CreateRenderPass2 path. In Vulkan without dynamic rendering you need to provide a \"compatible\" render pass when creating a graphics pipeline. Compatible passes need to have attachments that match the formats and *sample counts* of the eventual \"real\" render pass they will be used with. When using MSRTSS this means that attachments affected by the extension must have a sample count of 1 (even though it makes little sense from the point of view of the pipeline to know that? It will be rendering with N samples regardless of how the pass resolves. But I digress...)\n\nAt this point we don\u0027t have any data that we\u0027re providing at pipeline creation to inform it what the individual sample counts of the attachments are, we just have one count for the whole pipeline. In order to use MSRTSS _and_ CreateRenderPass2 we\u0027ll have to add something to indicate that to the pipeline descriptor. This feels silly to me, because we know that the drivers can generally work just fine without this data (as evidenced by the dynamic rendering path) but, well... Vulkan.\n\nSo, just to confirm: Do we want to add a signal to every attachment in the pipeline desc that it will be used with MSRTSS, even though we know that this will be useless data in a few years time when Vulkan 1.3 is more common, or do we want to say that you can only use MSRTSS with the dyanmic rendering path, which simply means the extension surfaces on less devices than it would have otherwise?",
      "revId": "2939f8e718ddc4c83fc36970992180f3aa14ac3d",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
