      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e When using MSRTSS this means that attachments affected by the extension must have a sample count of 1 (even though it makes little sense from the point of view of the pipeline to know that? It will be rendering with N samples regardless of how the pass resolves.\n\nSample count of 1 but also include `VkMultisampledRenderToSingleSampledInfoEXT` with N samples. You\u0027re right that render pass compatibility rules are too strict, they are too strict in too many aspects 😞 (this one being my fault)\n\nDoes Dawn allow mixing msrtss and non-msrtss attachments in the same render pass? If not, it\u0027s simpler, but you might as well at this point just ignore the validation error and set the sample count to N regardless of MSRTSS. You\u0027re right that the compiler only really cares about N.\n\n(Another VU you might want to ignore with legacy render pass objects is VUID-vkCmdExecuteCommands-pCommandBuffers-00099, because it doesn\u0027t take existence of resolve attachments into account)",
